Z||000009||avengador1||12-12-2001||09:12 PM||||Exotic Illutions, L.A.Concept Cars, D&R Replicars, all make Countach replica that fit on the stock wheelbase Fiero. Check them out at <A HREF="http://www.kitcar.com" TARGET=_blank>www.kitcar.com</A>The Mirage X is the only kit that I have seen that uses a stock wheelbase Fiero  .   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg">   <P>[This message has been edited by avengador1 (edited 12-12-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by avengador1 (edited 12-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||12-12-2001||09:28 PM||||No offense to Arch, but I still like the 'short' Diablo better. My preference is still the Countach though, short or long. I personally wouldnt do any kit that required stretching frame, but possibly a tube frame from scratch would be OK. If I did a 355, Id alter the wheel opening at rear to fit stock Fiero. Id rather move some glass 3", than add 3" to frame. Euroworks does some nice work, There only about 40 miles from me.||||reg||1
Z||000011||turbo86se||12-12-2001||09:40 PM||||Last year I got a letter from a company called Tropic Design. They make a Diablo stock Fiero rebody. It looks really, really good. They sent me pics but I can't find them. It's very affordable too. Their phone number is (819)324-0934. The letter I got came from Hugo Rodriquez, Marketing Coordinator and Co-owner. Give them a try. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SC.jpg"> ||||reg||1
